CI/CD Interview Experience | Real Conversation

Today in an interview, the discussion moved straight into CI/CD. Sharing a small part of how it went 👇

Interviewer: What is CI/CD in simple words?

Sanjit: CI/CD is about automation. Continuous Integration means every code change is automatically built and tested. Continuous Deployment means that validated code is released to environments automatically, reducing manual work and errors. ⚙️

Interviewer: How did you implement CI/CD in your projects?

Sanjit: I used Azure DevOps YAML pipelines. CI handled build, unit testing, and Docker image creation. CD handled deployment to AKS using Helm charts with proper environment separation. 🚢

Interviewer: What if the build fails?

Sanjit: The pipeline stops immediately and the team gets notified. Fixing issues early is the main goal of CI. 🛑

Interviewer: How do you handle secrets?

Sanjit: Secrets are stored securely in Azure Key Vault and accessed through service connections. No secrets are hardcoded. 🔐

Interviewer: How do you ensure zero downtime?

Sanjit: Using rolling deployments in Kubernetes along with readiness and liveness probes, users never face downtime. 📈

💡 My key takeaway
CI/CD is not just about tools, it is about building trust in every deployment.
